WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Create a Maven remote named maven-central. The URL is Maven Central, repo1.maven.org/maven2.

2
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Create a Maven repository with the same name, and leave Remote empty. For Maven, the remote belongs on the distribution.

3
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Create a Maven distribution. Name and base path are maven-central. Choose the maven-central repository. Open Pull-through caching and pick the maven-central remote.

4
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:41.000
This base URL is what clients use, like a Nexus repository URL. Client setup is ready to copy.

5
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Hosted repositories skip the remote. Create maven-releases, and set the base path to the same name.

6
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Create maven-snapshots the same way. Pulp keeps releases and snapshots as two repositories.

7
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:08.000
settings.xml mirrors Central to the Pulp cache. Read from the content URL. Deploy to the Maven upload URL.

8
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.000
mvn package downloads commons-lang3 and the build plugins through that cache.

9
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.000
In maven-central, Versions grew by one version for each cached file.

10
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:29.000
mvn deploy uploads hello-lib 1.0.0 to maven-releases. The snapshot went to maven-snapshots.

11
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Browse maven-releases and open hello-lib 1.0.0. Install shows the Maven and Gradle snippets.

12
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:49.400
Clear the local copy and run hello-app. Maven fetches hello-lib from Pulp, and the app prints Hello, Pulp.
